# Business Insights – E-commerce Analytics

## Revenue & Sales
- Monthly revenue shows a consistent upward trend, indicating growing customer demand.
- Electronics is the highest revenue-generating category, contributing the largest share of total sales.
- A small number of high-value orders contribute significantly to overall revenue.

## Customer Behavior
- Repeat customers generate more revenue than one-time customers, highlighting the importance of customer retention.
- Customer Lifetime Value (CLV) analysis helps identify high-value customers for targeted marketing campaigns.
- Major customer concentration comes from metro cities, suggesting strong urban demand.

## Orders & Operations
- Most orders are successfully completed, but a noticeable percentage are cancelled.
- Reducing order cancellations can directly improve revenue and customer satisfaction.
- Average Order Value (AOV) indicates opportunities for upselling and cross-selling strategies.

## Payments
- UPI and Card payments are the most preferred payment methods among customers.
- Optimizing the checkout experience for these payment modes can improve conversion rates.

## Business Recommendations
- Focus on retention strategies such as loyalty programs for repeat customers.
- Increase marketing efforts in high-revenue categories like Electronics.
- Analyze cancellation reasons to reduce lost revenue.
- Promote bundled products to increase Average Order Value.
